       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in PMR:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " sarilumab (IL-6 inhibitor) for inadequate response to corticosteroids or inability to tolerate a dose ↓; TNF inhibitors (infliximab, adalimumab) haven't shown benefit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) dose, polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PMR: 200 mg SC once every two wks in combination w a tapering course of systemic corticosteroids; may be used as monotherapy following discontinuation of corticosteroids."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infections that may lead to hospitalization or death; opportunistic infections also reported; avoid use in pts w an active infection. Prior to starting KEVZARA, test for latent TB; if positive, start treatment for TB."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to sarilumab or any of the inactive ingredients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) neutropenia/CBC screening:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ initiate KEVZARA in pts w ANC less than 2,000/mm3, platelets less than 150,000/mm3, or liver transaminases above 1.5 times ULN. Assess ANC prior to initiation and monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy and every 3 mo thereafter. Discontinue KEVZARA in PMR pts who develop neutropenia (ANC below 1,000 per mm3 at the end of the dosing interval), thrombocytopenia (platelets below 100,000 per mm3), or AST or ALT elevations 3 times above the ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) LFT monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Assess ALT and AST prior to initiation and monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy and every 3 mo thereafter; when clinically indicated, consider other LFTs such as bilirubin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) GI perforation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perforations reported, primarily as complications of diverticulitis; risk may be ↑ w concurrent diverticulitis or concomitant NSAIDs or corticosteroids; promptly evaluate pts presenting w new onset abdominal Sx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) live vaccines:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ concurrent use of live vaccines during treatment w KEVZARA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) CYP substrates:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Blockade of IL-6 signaling by IL-6Rα antagonists such as KEVZARA might reverse the inhibitory effect of IL-6 and restore CYP activity, leading to altered drug concentrations. On initiation or discontinuation of KEVZARA, perform therapeutic monitoring of effect (e.g., warfarin) or drug concentration (e.g., theophylline) and adjust the dose as needed. Exercise caution when co-administering KEVZARA w CYP3A4 substrate drugs where ↓ in effectiveness is undesirable, e.g., oral contraceptives, lovastatin, atorvastatin."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
